  "exec_summary": "The European Banking Authority has published a draft technical package of its reporting and disclosure framework, version 4.4, which is a significant development for EU financial institutions. In Belgium, there are no major regulatory developments this week, but the EU's crypto regulation, specifically the Markets in Crypto-Assets regulation, has been noted to bar Belarusian control of MiCA firms. The European Central Bank has also announced it will extend the use of climate factors in the Eurosystem collateral framework to non-financial corporate credit claims, and separately, will start implementing an enhanced repo facility for central banks.",
